course: dictionary
lesson: 10614
title: Acronyms and names in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: UNESCO is an acronym: a word made from the first letters of a longer name. The full name is the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization, and UNESCO is the short form. Capital letters tell you it is a name, not an ordinary word.
explain: Read the clues in «in 2022 UNESCO listed the culture of Ukrainian borshch cooking as heritage in need of urgent protection.» Listed and protection tell you UNESCO is an organization that chooses special things and helps keep them safe. Try your meaning in the sentence: does "an organization that chooses and protects special things" fit? It does.
explain: Once you know what UNESCO does, other sentences make more sense. «UNESCO also helps children get schooling» shows its work on education. Some places, like Stonehenge, are World Heritage Sites chosen by UNESCO because the whole world should protect them.
fact: UNESCO stands for United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization.
fact: UNESCO is part of the United Nations and works for education, science and culture around the world.
fact: UNESCO chooses World Heritage Sites: places so special that the whole world should protect them.
fact: UNESCO World Heritage Sites include the Great Wall of China, Stonehenge, the Grand Canyon, the Great Barrier Reef and the Giant's Causeway.
fact: «Borshch» is a red beetroot soup served with sour cream, and «borscht» is the same soup spelled differently in English.
exercise: «UNESCO listed the culture of Ukrainian borshch cooking as heritage in need of urgent protection.» What does UNESCO do here? | It sells soup to schools | *It chooses special things for the whole world to protect | It is a river in Ukraine | It is a red beetroot
exercise: Which short name is made from the first letters of the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization? | Borshch | Heritage | *UNESCO | Stonehenge
exercise: Which of these is an example of a UNESCO World Heritage Site? | Sour cream | *The Great Barrier Reef | The River Thames | A red beetroot soup
test: Which organization chooses World Heritage Sites? | Stonehenge | Borshch | *UNESCO | The Giant's Causeway
test: What does the word UNESCO stand for? | *United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization | United Nations Every Second Child | Universal National Education Office | United Nations Emergency Services
exam: «UNESCO also helps children get schooling.» What does UNESCO help children get? | Soup | Mud | Holidays | *Schooling
